# v1.0.54 (§1.6.50) PART 5 — default Excluded Apps seed list
#
# Format, one package name per line:
#
#   com.example.app            ← seeded on first run, IF it is installed
#   # anything after '#' is a comment
#
# Rules the loader enforces:
#   * blank lines and '#' comments are ignored;
#   * a line is used verbatim as an Android package name — no spaces, no
#     commas, no aliases;
#   * a package that is not installed on the device is SKIPPED, never
#     inserted as a phantom row;
#   * the seed runs at most ONCE per install (see SETTING_EXCLUDED_APPS_SEEDED),
#     so a user who later removes a seeded app does not get it back.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE IS CURRENTLY EMPTY OF ENTRIES ─────────────────────────
#
# The seed exists so that a fresh install already excludes the Iranian
# services the operator uses, instead of asking them to tick 20 boxes by hand.
# The package names themselves have to be read off the real device: the
# operator entered those apps manually on the phone, and the authoritative
# list lives there, not in this repository. Guessing package names from
# memory would produce rows that silently match nothing (or, worse, match the
# wrong app), and the seeder would then report success while excluding
# nothing.
#
# So this asset ships with the format and the loader in place and the entries
# pending. Adding them later is a data edit to this one file — no code change,
# no schema change, no migration — because the parsing, the installed check,
# the one-shot flag and the tests are already done.
#
# See the v1.0.54 report, DEFERRED item D1.
